      <h3>One caveat about our own formula</h3>

      <p>
        The zinc in Collabloom is 1.5mg, which is a supporting amount rather than a
        therapeutic one. The ICMR requirement for adults is around 12mg to 17mg a day
        depending on sex and diet, so a shot is not going to correct a genuine zinc
        shortfall. It sits alongside the collagen to make sure the enzymatic step is not
        left completely unsupported. If you suspect you are actually zinc deficient, get it
        tested and treat it properly rather than expecting a collagen shot to cover it.
        Collabloom is ₹1,899 for a month, and I would rather you knew what it does and does
        not do before you spend that.
      </p>

      <h3>A practical order of operations</h3>

      <ol>
        <li><strong>Sunscreen, daily, at the right quantity.</strong> Quarter teaspoon for face and neck, reapplied if you are outdoors. Nothing else on this list returns as much.</li>
        <li><strong>Count your protein for three days.</strong> Not forever. Just long enough to find out whether you are at 0.83g per kg or at half of it.</li>
        <li><strong>Get vitamin C from food, spread out.</strong> Amla, guava, capsicum, citrus. Aim for intake in the 100mg to 200mg range rather than the 40mg minimum.</li>
        <li><strong>Sleep seven hours.</strong> Free, and the most resisted item here.</li>
        <li><strong>Add a retinoid if your skin tolerates it.</strong> Low strength, two nights a week to start, always with sunscreen.</li>
        <li><strong>Then consider a collagen supplement.</strong> Check the milligrams, check for vitamin C, check the sugar content, and give it twelve weeks before you judge it.</li>
      </ol>

